                <pb facs="0848" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/249: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Child</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-18T15:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 18,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 19—1:34
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>60. Department’s number 50, April 15, 2 p.m. Foreign Office states that no more
                    deliveries will be made under contracts before or after joint declaration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Child</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
